0:{"buildId":"JFSdapXluxcZ7WLb1GQKv","data":[{"rsc":["$","$1","c",{"children":[["$","$L2",null,{"caseData":{"level":"RED","case_id":"R002","title":"The Canteen Complaint","short_summary":"A disturbing lunch-tray photo reaches school staff with a demand for an immediate response before the story spreads.","duration_min":12,"skills":["Visual evidence","Language and claims","Information chains"],"spotted_url":"/assets/images/R002/R002_spotted.png","theme":["School life","Food safety"],"story_context":"An anonymous message includes a canteen photo and warns that it will be shared publicly unless the school responds before a deadline. Staff must determine what the image and wording actually support before taking action.","modules":{"step_1_image_forensics":{"mechanic_type":"IMAGE_FORENSICS","image_url":"/assets/images/R002/R002_fake.png","image_width":1020,"image_height":680,"context_text":"The leaked image attached to the extortion email claims to show 'a disgusting cockroach served in the high school canteen food tray.'","target_anomalies":[{"anomaly_id":"R002_IMG_01","name":"fake_cockroach_insertion","x_pct":69.5,"y_pct":73,"radius_pct":13.5,"socratic_quiz":{"question":"Which comparison would best test whether the cockroach belongs naturally in this scene?","options":["A. Measure its length against several grains of rice to decide whether that species could exist.","B. Compare its color transitions, surface texture, and highlights with the nearby food and metal under the same light.","C. Count how many separate food items appear in the tray around it."],"correct_option":"B","explanation":"Size varies by species and perspective. Material and lighting differences under the same conditions are a stronger comparison, but the source still needs checking."},"description":"The cockroach has unusually saturated, polished coloring and a toy-like surface that does not respond to the scene's light like the rice and metal tray."}]},"step_2_text_highlight":{"mechanic_type":"TEXT_HIGHLIGHT","simulated_post":{"author":"Anonymous","time_posted":"5 hour ago","content":"I don't usually post stuff like this, but today's lunch honestly made me uncomfortable. While I was eating, I noticed what looked like a cockroach in my lunch tray. I don't know whether it came from the kitchen or somewhere else, maybe there's a perfectly good explanation out there, but if this really came from the cafeteria, students have a right to be worried. I'm not saying the cafeteria is unsafe. I'm just asking why this keeps happening and why nobody ever seems to explain anything afterward. The school seems to never take students' food feedback into consideration anyway, saying the problem is too complicated or something like that. At this point, I think parents deserve to know what's happening before this gets quietly swept under the rug..."},"traps":[{"trap_id":"R002_TRAP_01","ground_truth_start":365,"ground_truth_end":502,"matched_text":"I'm not saying the cafeteria is unsafe. I'm just asking why this keeps happening and why nobody ever seems to explain anything afterward.","weapon_type":["seeding_doubt"],"socratic_quiz":{"question":"What evidence would be needed before 'why this keeps happening' becomes a fair question?","options":["A. The author's uncertainty about where the insect came from.","B. Independently verified earlier incidents showing that the same problem has actually recurred.","C. The absence of an immediate reply beneath this particular post."],"correct_option":"B","explanation":"The phrase 'keeps happening' turns one unverified case into a pattern. That claim requires several independently verified incidents."}},{"trap_id":"R002_TRAP_02","ground_truth_start":503,"ground_truth_end":646,"matched_text":"The school seems to never take students' food feedback into consideration anyway, saying the problem is too complicated or something like that.","weapon_type":["poisoning_the_well","overgeneralization"],"socratic_quiz":{"question":"How could a reader evaluate a future school response without inheriting the post's framing?","options":["A. Judge the response by how many commenters already distrust the school.","B. Examine its evidence and reasoning before deciding whether complexity is genuine or merely an excuse.","C. Reject the response if it contains technical details that are difficult to understand."],"correct_option":"B","explanation":"The post labels any future response an excuse before it exists. Judge the response by its evidence, not by this advance framing."}},{"trap_id":"R002_TRAP_03","ground_truth_start":647,"ground_truth_end":758,"matched_text":"At this point, I think parents deserve to know what's happening before this gets quietly swept under the rug...","weapon_type":["conspiracy_theory","appeal_to_fear"],"socratic_quiz":{"question":"How does 'before this gets quietly swept under the rug' change the order in which readers act and verify?","options":["A. It makes immediate sharing feel protective, moving escalation ahead of checking whether a cover-up exists.","B. It limits the claim to one personal observation and reduces pressure to act.","C. It directs readers to an independent source before they form a judgment."],"correct_option":"A","explanation":"The implied cover-up introduces a conspiracy narrative and appeals to fear, making rapid sharing feel safer than waiting. That artificial urgency reverses a sound verification order: readers are pushed to amplify first and investigate later."}}]},"step_3_sorting_game":{"mechanic_type":"DRAG_AND_DROP_SORTING","context_text":"A misleading social media post about the school canteen has spread across the community.","pool_items":[{"item_id":"R002_SORT_01","text":"Other users repost the image with stronger claims, assuming the worst."},{"item_id":"R002_SORT_02","text":"The rumor becomes accepted as 'common knowledge' even though the original claim was never confirmed."},{"item_id":"R002_SORT_03","text":"Someone uploads a photo with a personal interpretation but without verified context."},{"item_id":"R002_SORT_04","text":"People react emotionally and share the post before waiting for official verification."}],"correct_sequence":["R002_SORT_03","R002_SORT_01","R002_SORT_04","R002_SORT_02"],"validation_feedback":{"success":"Correct. Rumors often become believable through repetition rather than evidence. An unverified observation can evolve into 'everyone knows it's true' as people add assumptions, share emotionally, and stop checking the original source.","failure":"Not quite. False information rarely spreads because of one convincing post alone. It gains momentum as people amplify unverified claims and repeat them as facts before anyone verifies the evidence."}}},"dialogue_trigger":{"question":"Ask your Teacher/Parent: If you received this message, what evidence would you need before believing the photo reflects a real food safety problem rather than a manipulated story?","mil_insight":"A single image rarely provides enough context to establish what happened. Discuss how to distinguish direct evidence from assumptions by checking the original source, verifying when and where the photo was taken, and following the school's official investigation process before drawing conclusions."}}}],["$L3","$L4","$L5"],"$L6"]}],"isPartial":"$@7","staleTime":"$8","varyParams":null},{"rsc":"$L9","isPartial":"$@a","staleTime":"$8","varyParams":null},{"rsc":"$Lb","isPartial":"$@c","staleTime":"$8","varyParams":"$d"},{"rsc":"$Le","isPartial":"$@f","staleTime":"$8","varyParams":"$d"}],"isUpgradeableISRFallback":false,"a":"$@10","rootVaryParams":null,"needsRuntimeRequest":"$@11"}
